// SimCam — signing configuration for the host menubar app + system extension.
//
// Why this file exists
// --------------------
// macOS TCC (Privacy & Security) ties permission grants to the app's code
// signing **designated requirement** (anchor cert + bundle id), not to the
// cdhash. With pure ad-hoc signing (`codesign -s -`) every rebuild produces
// a new cdhash AND there is no anchor certificate, so TCC treats every build
// as a brand new app and the user has to re-grant Screen Recording / Camera /
// Microphone every single time.
//
// Apple DTS confirms this on:
//   https://developer.apple.com/forums/thread/819406
//   https://developer.apple.com/forums/thread/678816
// Quinn's verdict: "to work well with TCC you need to sign your code with a
// stable identity, typically an Apple-issued code signing identity".
//
// Free Apple IDs already provide one: the "Apple Development" certificate that
// Xcode auto-creates when you add an Apple ID under Settings -> Accounts and
// pick the "Personal Team" -> "Sign to Run Locally" option. That is enough to
// make TCC grants persist across rebuilds.
//
// How this file works
// -------------------
// project.yml references SIMCAM_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM and SIMCAM_CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY.
// They default below to ad-hoc (so unconfigured forks still build), and you
// override them in Configs/SimCamSigning.local.xcconfig (gitignored) with your
// own personal team id. SimCamHook (iOS dylib) and SimCamDemoApp (iOS demo)
// stay ad-hoc unconditionally — the iOS Simulator's dyld will not load a
// dylib signed with an "Apple Development" cert into an ad-hoc-signed host
// process, so any team config there breaks injection.
//
// To configure your machine:
//   1. cp Configs/SimCamSigning.local.xcconfig.template Configs/SimCamSigning.local.xcconfig
//   2. edit and put in your team id (Xcode -> Settings -> Accounts -> your
//      Apple ID -> Manage Certificates -> the 10-char team id in parens).
//   3. xcodegen generate && open SimCam.xcodeproj  (Xcode will pick up the
//      identity automatically).
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Default to ad-hoc so a fresh clone without any local config still builds.
SIMCAM_CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = -
SIMCAM_CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Manual
SIMCAM_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =

// Pull in the user's local override if it exists. xcconfig #include with a
// leading "?" makes the include optional, so missing files are not an error.
#include? "SimCamSigning.local.xcconfig"
